-- title:
--   Non-Gauss minimal prime over p as Atkin–Lehner branch
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$ and a nonzero $M$ with $p \mid M$ and $p^{2} \nmid M$, and a subgroup $H \le (\mathbb Z/M)^{\times}$ containing every unit whose image under `ZMod.unitsMap` for $(M/p) \mid M$ is $1$; assume `jqModC ℚ` lies in `qExpFunctionFieldC ℚ ⊤`. Write $F =$ `qExpFunctionFieldC ℚ (CohCarrier.GammaH M H)`, the subfield of $\mathbb Q$-Laurent series generated over $\mathbb Q$ by the relevant intermediate-form ratios at the level `GammaH M H` (the image in $\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb Z)$ of the preimage of $H$ under $\Gamma_0(M) \to (\mathbb Z/M)^{\times}$). Let $\sigma$ be a $\mathbb Q$-algebra automorphism of $F$ such that (i) whenever $f \in F$ agrees as a Laurent series with an element $u$ of the field of level `GammaH (M/p) (infSubgroup p M H hpM)` — the level attached to the image of $H$ in $(\mathbb Z/(M/p))^{\times}$ — one has $\sigma f =$ `qExpand ℚ p` $u$, i.e. $q \mapsto q^{p}$; and (ii) for every unit $c$ of $\mathbb Z/(M/p)$ with underlying residue $p$, whenever $f$ equals `qExpand ℚ p` $u$ as a Laurent series, the coefficientwise embedding of $\sigma f$ into Laurent series over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ equals `diamondAutHBar (M / p) (infSubgroup p M H hpM) c` applied to the corresponding element of `xHFunctionFieldBar (M / p) (infSubgroup p M H hpM)`. Let $W_0$ be a valuation subring of $F$ whose members are exactly the $f$ for which there are power series $a, a'$ over the subring of rationals with denominator coprime to $p$, with $a'$ nonzero modulo $p$ under [`GaloisRep.ratLocalizedAtResidue p`](def/GaloisRep_RatLocalizedAtResidue.html#L15), such that $f \cdot a' = a$ as Laurent series. Let $P$ be an ideal of `chartAlgInf p (CohCarrier.GammaH M H) hj`, the subalgebra of $F$ of elements integral over the subalgebra generated over the base ring `R p` by the inverse of `jAt`, and suppose $P$ is a minimal prime over the ideal generated by $p$ there, and that some $b \in P$ has image in $F$ outside the nonunits of $W_0$. Then for every $b$ in that subalgebra, $b \in P$ if and only if the image of $b$ in $F$ lies in the nonunits of $W_0$ pulled back along $\sigma$, i.e. in the maximal ideal of $\sigma^{-1}(W_0)$.
--
--   The mod-$p$ fibre of the pole chart of the two-chart integral model of $X_H(M)$ at a prime exactly dividing the level has two components; this statement identifies the minimal prime other than the Gauss one as the centre of the valuation ring obtained from the Gauss ring by the Atkin–Lehner substitution $q \mapsto q^{p}$ together with a diamond twist. It is used in [`ModularCurve.XHDRModelAtP.not_isInftySide_of_section_comp_one`](thm.html#ModularCurve.XHDRModelAtP.not_isInftySide_of_section_comp_one).
